WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.910
Welcome to the Oxendine Painting
demonstration, built by Catalyst

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.070
Innovations. This is the actual
application running with fictional sample

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.090
information. We will follow one estimate
from its scope through pricing and

4
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.550
review. Start with the areas of the job.

5
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.270
Each room keeps its work, preparation, and
estimated hours together,

6
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.390
so the scope is easier to review.

7
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.890
When the work changes, update the area
rather than searching through a

8
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.710
separate document. Next, open pricing.

9
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:32.710
Here, the estimate connects labor and
material costs with the work being

10
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.970
quoted. Review the line items alongside
the summary, and see how

11
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:38.950
the entered assumptions affect the
estimate.

12
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.370
These figures are sample inputs, not
promised business results.

13
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.510
Finally, move to review. Check the costs
and estimated margin

14
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.830
before the customer handoff. This is a
demonstration prototype for a

15
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.970
planned system; approval and sending are
simulated.

16
00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.290
The useful idea is simple: keep the scope,
the costs, and the next step

17
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.190
together. Talk with Catalyst about
connecting the work in your business.

